{%- comment -%}
  MONOCHROME order confirmation: "The Evidence Locker". The (fictional) Monochrome Bureau logs the order as evidence: a RECEIVED
  stamp, a case plate with the facts, one sealed bag + exhibit tag per item, a thermal evidence receipt, the extraction point and
  an honest chain of custody. Every piece of order data is live text; the images are props.
  Install: Shopify admin > Settings > Notifications > Order confirmation > Edit code > select all, replace with this file >
  Preview > Save. "Revert to default" on the same screen brings Shopify's own template back.
  Images: img/oc-*.png|gif, rendered by make_images.mjs. Their src paths start with the NIMG placeholder, which the build step
  (build.py) replaces with the Shopify CDN URLs from img-urls.json, writing dist/order-confirmation.liquid: paste that one.
  The room colour #171717 is baked into the bag, tag and receipt edges, #0d0d0d into the wordmark plate: change them together.
  The VISION10 slip shows only when the order contains The Vision Issue (product 15418664059134).
  Layout is mobile-first: the inline styles alone fit a 320px phone (Gmail's app drops the <style> block for non-Google
  accounts); the media queries only refine it, and min-width 621px / the mso block restore the 40px desktop margins.
  Shopify semantics followed from its default template: shipping_price is BEFORE shipping discounts; has_pending_payment
  orders get "received", not "confirmed"; delivery_method 'pick-up' / 'local'; duties and tips are part of total_price.
  Before going live, place one test order with VISION10 and one with free shipping and check the receipt adds up.
{%- endcomment -%}
